From: turbo-boo <59400127+turbo-boo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 17:50:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] leaudio: Use one CIS per channel for ADSP offloaded stereo
 headsets

A single LE Audio device that supports two channels per ASE gets the
STEREO_ONE_CIS_PER_DEVICE strategy, so both channels share one CIS. The
QTI ADSP offload path counts the active stream map entries as the
encoder channel count, configures the BLE device as mono and the
listener hears a downmix duplicated on both sides.

When the codec runs on the ADSP and the device exposes at least two
sink ASEs, use STEREO_TWO_CISES_PER_DEVICE so every channel gets its own
CIS, as the offload path expects.
---
 system/bta/le_audio/device_groups.cc | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/system/bta/le_audio/device_groups.cc b/system/bta/le_audio/device_groups.cc
index 69e444e..d9267b1 100644
--- a/system/bta/le_audio/device_groups.cc
+++ b/system/bta/le_audio/device_groups.cc
@@ -1433,6 +1433,16 @@ types::LeAudioConfigurationStrategy LeAudioDeviceGroup::GetGroupSinkStrategy() c
         return types::LeAudioConfigurationStrategy::STEREO_TWO_CISES_PER_DEVICE;
       }
 
+      /* The QTI ADSP offload path derives the encoder channel count from the
+       * number of active CISes, so two channels on a single CIS are downmixed
+       * to mono. Use one CIS per channel when the device has an ASE for each.
+       */
+      if (direction == types::kLeAudioDirectionSink &&
+          CodecManager::GetInstance()->GetCodecLocation() == types::CodecLocation::ADSP &&
+          device->GetAseCount(direction) >= 2) {
+        return types::LeAudioConfigurationStrategy::STEREO_TWO_CISES_PER_DEVICE;
+      }
+
       return types::LeAudioConfigurationStrategy::STEREO_ONE_CIS_PER_DEVICE;
     };
     strategy_ = strategy_selector(types::kLeAudioDirectionSink);
